Baptiste,

As a worst-case workaround, I have noticed that labels= will accept the "\n" newline character. You could do something like:

qplot (x, y) + scale_x_continuous("X Stuff", breaks=c(0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0), labels=c("12\n13", "10\n15", "5\n12", "20\b\n04"))

to get apparently two numbers at each tick mark. So in your example of Celusius and Farenheit, you'd have to make one the primary item (nice even numbers) and derive the second at the same points (would not be nice even numbers).

Just a thought

   Wayne

